- 50 fichiers Vitest, 264 tests : ✅
- TypeScript application et Node : ✅
- ESLint ciblé et formatage : ✅
- build de production : ✅
- audit des dépendances de production : aucune vulnérabilité connue ✅
- invariants frontend, CI, Vercel et SQL : ✅
- migration et test SQL diagnostics sur le staging canonique : ✅
- preview réelle : 6 intégrations opérationnelles sur 6, 0 échec ✅

La CI GitHub complète est verte, notamment le typecheck des huit fonctions Edge et leurs tests de sécurité. Le build Vercel du dernier commit a été refusé uniquement par le quota de builds; la preview exécutable précédente, identique côté runtime, est READY et validée 6/6.

## Summary

Establishes the architecture foundation for the tile planning microservice before UI implementation.

## Included

- deep-module graph in `architecture/app-architecture.yaml`;
- explicit service ownership and integration boundaries;
- initial durable domain model for projects, materials, layouts, surface references, impacts, and tile operations;
- source revision and stale-calculation workflow;
- implementation order aligned with `svg-engineering-editors-skills`;
- README describing scope and architectural rules.

## Key decisions

- canonical geometry remains owned by the geometry service;
- plumbing and electrical integrations use normalized surface impacts;
- the tile planner owns tile-specific interpretations and quantities;
- reference images are represented by stable asset IDs and appearance settings;
- SVG and derived tile polygons are not persisted as project data;
- estimate pricing remains outside this service.

## Not included

- framework selection;
- dependency installation;
- UI implementation;
- executable TypeScript contracts;
- tiling or texture algorithms.

These should follow after the architecture graph is reviewed and stabilized.

